1
00:00:00,589 --> 00:00:03,710
Let's see how we can create the shared VPC.

2
00:00:03,890 --> 00:00:05,590
Let's go to the Google admin console.

3
00:00:05,789 --> 00:00:10,960
For shared VPC, we will make one project, and we make it as a host.

4
00:00:11,189 --> 00:00:13,340
So let's click here and say New project.

5
00:00:13,510 --> 00:00:18,229
I call it ps‑example‑host, say Create.

6
00:00:18,469 --> 00:00:22,630
Now I'm going to create a shared VPC within this host.

7
00:00:22,630 --> 00:00:25,120
And I have two separate projects,

8
00:00:25,270 --> 00:00:29,510
and what I'm trying to do is I'm going to create an instance in

9
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:33,229
each of those two projects and show how they can talk to each

10
00:00:33,229 --> 00:00:35,990
other without sharing actually anything.

11
00:00:36,270 --> 00:00:41,470
Now, inside this project, go to the VPC network and go to the Shared VPC.

12
00:00:41,790 --> 00:00:45,409
Now click on Set up Shared VPC, say Enable and continue.

13
00:00:45,669 --> 00:00:50,180
So it got enabled, now it is working, and say Continue and say Save.

14
00:00:50,389 --> 00:00:57,120
Now let's go to the VPC network and Create, now give a name as corp‑vpc‑ps.

15
00:00:58,520 --> 00:00:59,939
I keep everything as it is.

16
00:01:00,139 --> 00:01:03,810
Give a name for subnet, vpc‑subnet‑ps.

17
00:01:04,132 --> 00:01:05,611
It will ask to select the region,

18
00:01:05,851 --> 00:01:10,972
so I select the region, and I will select the IP range and say Create.

19
00:01:11,491 --> 00:01:15,171
Now we have created a VPC which has the subnet.

20
00:01:15,762 --> 00:01:18,391
Now I have two already projects.

21
00:01:18,611 --> 00:01:22,732
One is hpc3 and another one is hpc2.

22
00:01:23,012 --> 00:01:27,891
Now what I'm going to do is I'm going to attach both of these projects to my

23
00:01:27,891 --> 00:01:31,853
shared VPC. I have to just come down here to Shared VPC,

24
00:01:32,033 --> 00:01:37,954
and within the Shared VPC, I click on Attached projects and say Attach projects.

25
00:01:38,153 --> 00:01:39,543
Now let me select the project.

26
00:01:39,674 --> 00:01:42,874
I'm selecting here hpc2, say Save.

27
00:01:43,113 --> 00:01:47,314
Similarly, adding one more project, that is hpc3.

28
00:01:47,433 --> 00:01:51,353
Now what I'm going to do is I'm going to create one

29
00:01:51,353 --> 00:01:55,916
instance in hpc2 and another instance in hpc3,

30
00:01:55,966 --> 00:02:00,886
and I will show you how both of these two different machines from two

31
00:02:00,886 --> 00:02:05,015
different projects talk to each other because of the shared VPC.

32
00:02:05,255 --> 00:02:06,496
Go to hpc2.

33
00:02:06,615 --> 00:02:08,535
I'm adding one compute machine.

34
00:02:08,695 --> 00:02:11,755
Say Create instance, selecting the region,

35
00:02:11,856 --> 00:02:14,485
and importantly, under the Networking,

36
00:02:14,535 --> 00:02:19,229
I'm going to select the network, which is already shared with me,

37
00:02:19,250 --> 00:02:23,869
and under that I'm going to select the subnet and say Create.

38
00:02:24,009 --> 00:02:26,679
Now this network option, if you are seeing it,

39
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:29,570
that means your project is correctly attached.

40
00:02:29,690 --> 00:02:34,690
Now, similarly, in another tab, I'm selecting the hpc3 project.

41
00:02:34,809 --> 00:02:37,759
I'm going to create a compute engine as well,

42
00:02:37,839 --> 00:02:42,440
selecting the region and again under the networking here also,

43
00:02:42,490 --> 00:02:47,540
I'll be able to see the network interface that is shared with me,

44
00:02:47,540 --> 00:02:52,270
ps‑example‑host project and subnet is called vpc‑subnet.

45
00:02:52,410 --> 00:02:55,179
Again, I'll do the same thing, say Create here.

46
00:02:55,330 --> 00:02:58,449
Now both of these two instances get created.

47
00:02:58,649 --> 00:03:00,250
One is in project 2.

48
00:03:00,389 --> 00:03:02,570
Another one is in project 3.

49
00:03:02,919 --> 00:03:08,160
Now let me come down here and say SSH for this project 2 one.

50
00:03:08,309 --> 00:03:12,190
The internal IP address for project 2 is 10.10.0.4.

51
00:03:12,410 --> 00:03:15,440
The authorized will be able to do SSH.

52
00:03:15,679 --> 00:03:17,440
Now go down to the project 3.

53
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:20,419
So I'm doing the SSH inside this as well.

54
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:23,440
The IP address for this is 10.10.0.5.

55
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:24,600
Say Authorize.

56
00:03:24,839 --> 00:03:28,679
Now this is the window of our project 3 instance.

57
00:03:29,309 --> 00:03:33,960
Now I'm doing here ping and call 10.10.0.4.

58
00:03:34,119 --> 00:03:37,559
That is, I'm pinging the instance which is in the project 2,

59
00:03:37,679 --> 00:03:40,679
and you can see that it is able to talk to that.

60
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:45,000
Now on similar lines, I'm coming down to this project 2 instance,

61
00:03:45,190 --> 00:03:50,990
and here I'm saying ping 10.10.0.5, the machine which is in the project 3,

62
00:03:51,110 --> 00:03:54,210
and you can see that from project instance, I can

63
00:03:54,389 --> 00:03:56,339
talk to the project 3 instance.

64
00:03:56,509 --> 00:03:59,539
So both of these are able to talk to each other because

65
00:04:00,419 --> 00:04:03,929
they are sharing the common shared VPC,

66
00:04:04,029 --> 00:04:09,059
and that's how in the real‑world when projects have multiple microservices,

67
00:04:09,149 --> 00:04:13,330
so those projects talk to each other by having the shared network.
